---
import CourseSlideLayout from '../../../../layouts/CourseSlideLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../../../utils/paths';
import '../../../../styles/dedc02-literature-review.css';

const title = '4. Research Design & Alignment · DEDC02';
const description = 'An interactive lesson on frameworks, research design, sampling, validity, trustworthiness and methodological alignment.';
const courseHref = withBase('/teaching/courses/dedc02');
---

<CourseSlideLayout {title} {description}>
  <section class="pdf-cover" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="eyebrow">DEDC02 · Advanced Research Method</span>
    <h1>Research Design<br />&amp; Alignment</h1>
    <div class="pdf-message-block">
      <h2>Personal message</h2>
      <p data-pdf-message-print></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="top-tools" aria-label="Language and timer controls">
    <button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-global-translate>中文</button>
    <div class="compact-timer" aria-label="Activity timer">
      <input type="number" min="0.1" step="0.5" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="Timer" aria-label="Timer duration" data-timer-minutes />
      <output data-timer-output hidden aria-live="polite">00:00</output>
      <button type="button" data-timer-start>Start</button>
      <button type="button" data-timer-reset aria-label="Reset timer">↻</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="deck" aria-label="Research Design and Alignment slide deck">
    <section class="slide is-active" data-title="Research Design & Alignment" aria-hidden="false">
      <div class="slide-inner title-slide">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">DEDC02 · Advanced Research Method</span></header>
        <div class="title-rule"></div>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h1>Research Design<br />&amp; Alignment</h1>
          <p class="lead">Conceptual and theoretical frameworks, design families, sampling, validity, trustworthiness and the logic connecting them.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h1>研究設計<br />與對齊</h1>
          <p class="lead">概念與理論框架、研究設計類型、抽樣、效度、可信度，以及連結這些元素的邏輯。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Learning aims" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Where we are going</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>By the end, you can…</h2>
          <ol class="number-list">
            <li><span><strong>Distinguish</strong> a theoretical framework from a conceptual framework.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Select</strong> a design family that fits the question and intended claim.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Justify</strong> an initial sampling strategy.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Plan</strong> suitable validity or trustworthiness safeguards.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Audit</strong> the alignment of a proposed study.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>完成本課後，你可以⋯⋯</h2>
          <ol class="number-list">
            <li><span><strong>區分</strong>理論框架與概念框架。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>選擇</strong>符合研究問題與預期主張的設計類型。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>論證</strong>初步抽樣策略。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>規劃</strong>合適的效度或可信度保障。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>審視</strong>擬議研究的方法論對齊。</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="From gap to design" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Bridge from Week 3</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>A gap does not choose the method</h2>
          <div class="path-line design-chain">
            <span>Problem</span><b>→</b><span>Framework</span><b>→</b><span>Question</span><b>→</b><span>Claim</span>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">The design begins when you decide what evidence would make the intended answer defensible.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究缺口不會自動決定方法</h2>
          <div class="path-line design-chain">
            <span>研究課題</span><b>→</b><span>框架</span><b>→</b><span>研究問題</span><b>→</b><span>主張</span>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">當你開始判斷需要甚麼證據，才能使預期答案站得住腳，研究設計便開始了。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="What theory does" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Frameworks</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Theory gives the study an explanatory lens</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Select</h3><p>Identifies concepts and processes worth attending to.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Relate</h3><p>Proposes how concepts or conditions connect.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Explain</h3><p>Offers a reason why an observed pattern may occur.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Bound</h3><p>Makes assumptions and limits visible.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">A theory is more than a named citation. It must do identifiable work in the study.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>理論為研究提供解釋視角</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>選取</h3><p>指出值得關注的概念與過程。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>連結</h3><p>提出概念或條件之間可能如何關聯。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>解釋</h3><p>說明為何可能出現某種觀察模式。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>界定</h3><p>使假設與限制變得可見。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">理論不只是文獻中的一個名稱；它必須在研究中發揮可辨識的作用。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Theoretical and conceptual frameworks" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">The central distinction</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>One study, two levels of framework</h2>
          <div class="framework-study-source">
            <p><strong>Li (2025)</strong> · 206 secondary EFL learners · one argumentative L2 writing task · structural equation modelling</p>
            <div class="framework-study-links" aria-label="Study links">
              <a href="https://pressto.amu.edu.pl/index.php/ssllt/article/download/43371/38183/111749" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Download PDF <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="framework-workbench">
            <article class="framework-panel theory-panel">
              <div class="framework-panel-head">
                <span class="framework-role">Explains why</span>
                <h3>Theoretical framework</h3>
                <p>Control–Value Theory supplies the general explanatory chain.</p>
              </div>
              <ol class="theory-chain" aria-label="Control-Value Theory chain reconstructed from the study">
                <li><strong>Distal antecedents</strong><span>Personal factors · task environment</span></li>
                <li><strong>Proximal appraisals</strong><span>Perceived control · value</span></li>
                <li><strong>Achievement emotions</strong><span>Feelings arising around achievement</span></li>
                <li><strong>Achievement outcomes</strong><span>Performance and learning</span></li>
              </ol>
              <p class="framework-caption">Theory-level reconstruction from Li’s discussion of Control–Value Theory.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="framework-panel concept-panel">
              <div class="framework-panel-head">
                <span class="framework-role">Specifies what</span>
                <h3>Conceptual framework</h3>
                <p>The study selects task-level constructs and proposes testable paths.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="concept-model" aria-label="Li's conceptual framework: task control, intrinsic task value and extrinsic task value predict task emotions; task emotions predict L2 writing task performance; task control and extrinsic task value also have direct paths to performance">
                <div class="appraisal-stack">
                  <span>Task control</span>
                  <span>Intrinsic task value</span>
                  <span>Extrinsic task value</span>
                </div>
                <b class="concept-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</b>
                <div class="concept-node emotion-node"><strong>Task emotions</strong><span>Enjoyment · Anxiety · Boredom</span></div>
                <b class="concept-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</b>
                <div class="concept-node performance-node"><strong>L2 writing task performance</strong><span>Language · Content · Organisation</span></div>
              </div>
              <p class="direct-paths"><span>Task control</span><span>Extrinsic task value</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><strong>direct paths to performance</strong></p>
              <p class="framework-caption">Adapted from the paper’s Figure 2; arrows represent hypothesised relationships, not causal findings.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway framework-takeaway"><strong>The distinction:</strong> the theory supplies the explanatory logic; the conceptual framework operationalises that logic for this study.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>同一項研究，兩個框架層次</h2>
          <div class="framework-study-source">
            <p><strong>Li（2025）</strong>· 206 名中學 EFL 學習者 · 一項 L2 議論文寫作任務 · 結構方程模型</p>
            <div class="framework-study-links" aria-label="研究連結">
              <a href="https://pressto.amu.edu.pl/index.php/ssllt/article/download/43371/38183/111749" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">下載 PDF <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="framework-workbench">
            <article class="framework-panel theory-panel">
              <div class="framework-panel-head">
                <span class="framework-role">解釋「為甚麼」</span>
                <h3>理論框架</h3>
                <p>控制—價值理論提供一般性的解釋鏈。</p>
              </div>
              <ol class="theory-chain" aria-label="根據研究重構的控制—價值理論鏈">
                <li><strong>遠端前因</strong><span>個人因素 · 任務環境</span></li>
                <li><strong>近端評估</strong><span>知覺控制 · 價值</span></li>
                <li><strong>成就情緒</strong><span>圍繞成就活動產生的感受</span></li>
                <li><strong>成就結果</strong><span>表現與學習</span></li>
              </ol>
              <p class="framework-caption">根據 Li 對控制—價值理論的討論重構理論層次。</p>
            </article>

            <article class="framework-panel concept-panel">
              <div class="framework-panel-head">
                <span class="framework-role">具體說明「研究甚麼」</span>
                <h3>概念框架</h3>
                <p>研究選取任務層次構念，並提出可檢驗的路徑。</p>
              </div>
              <div class="concept-model" aria-label="Li 的概念框架：任務控制、任務內在價值與任務外在價值預測任務情緒；任務情緒預測第二語言寫作任務表現；任務控制與任務外在價值亦直接連結表現">
                <div class="appraisal-stack">
                  <span>任務控制</span>
                  <span>任務內在價值</span>
                  <span>任務外在價值</span>
                </div>
                <b class="concept-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</b>
                <div class="concept-node emotion-node"><strong>任務情緒</strong><span>愉悅 · 焦慮 · 無聊</span></div>
                <b class="concept-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</b>
                <div class="concept-node performance-node"><strong>L2 寫作任務表現</strong><span>語言 · 內容 · 組織</span></div>
              </div>
              <p class="direct-paths"><span>任務控制</span><span>任務外在價值</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><strong>直接連結任務表現</strong></p>
              <p class="framework-caption">改編自論文圖 2；箭咀代表假設關係，而非因果研究結果。</p>
            </article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway framework-takeaway"><strong>兩者之別：</strong>理論提供解釋邏輯；概念框架把該邏輯操作化為本研究要檢驗的關係。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 1: Framework Match" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 1</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Framework Match</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Match each statement to its function. Then defend the distinction with your group.</p>
          <div class="interactive-stack" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Social cognitive theory explains how beliefs, action and environment influence one another.</p><select data-answer="theory"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="theory">Theoretical framework</option><option value="concept">Conceptual framework</option><option value="neither">Neither</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Teacher feedback → learner self-efficacy → revision persistence, with prior achievement as a contextual condition.</p><select data-answer="concept"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="theory">Theoretical framework</option><option value="concept">Conceptual framework</option><option value="neither">Neither</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>“Students use AI because it is convenient.”</p><select data-answer="neither"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="theory">Theoretical framework</option><option value="concept">Conceptual framework</option><option value="neither">Neither</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>A diagram specifies which forms of AI literacy may relate to research confidence in this study.</p><select data-answer="concept"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="theory">Theoretical framework</option><option value="concept">Conceptual framework</option><option value="neither">Neither</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>Check matches</button><button type="button" data-clear>Clear</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>框架配對</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">把每項陳述配對至相應功能，再與小組解釋你的判斷。</p>
          <div class="interactive-stack" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>社會認知理論解釋信念、行動與環境如何互相影響。</p><select data-answer="theory"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="theory">理論框架</option><option value="concept">概念框架</option><option value="neither">兩者皆非</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>教師回饋 → 學習者自我效能 → 修訂堅持，並把先前成績視為情境條件。</p><select data-answer="concept"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="theory">理論框架</option><option value="concept">概念框架</option><option value="neither">兩者皆非</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>「學生使用人工智能，因為它很方便。」</p><select data-answer="neither"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="theory">理論框架</option><option value="concept">概念框架</option><option value="neither">兩者皆非</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>一個圖表指出本研究中哪些人工智能素養可能與研究信心有關。</p><select data-answer="concept"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="theory">理論框架</option><option value="concept">概念框架</option><option value="neither">兩者皆非</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>檢查配對</button><button type="button" data-clear>清除</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Framework to research question" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">From explanation to inquiry</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Let the framework sharpen the question</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Deductive use</h3><p>An existing theory supports propositions or hypotheses that the study tests.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Sensitising use</h3><p>A framework directs initial attention without fixing what qualitative inquiry must find.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Generative use</h3><p>Patterns in data support refinement or development of a conceptual or theoretical account.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Name the role of the framework. Do not claim to “use” a theory if it never shapes the question, evidence or interpretation.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>讓框架使研究問題更精準</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>演繹用途</h3><p>既有理論支持研究要檢驗的命題或假設。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>啟發用途</h3><p>框架引導初步注意，但不預先規定質性研究必須發現甚麼。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>生成用途</h3><p>資料模式支持修訂或發展概念／理論解釋。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">清楚說明框架扮演的角色。若理論從未影響問題、證據或詮釋，便不應聲稱研究「使用」了該理論。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Research design and its components" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Research architecture</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>A design coordinates the whole study</h2>
          <blockquote class="design-architecture-question">How will this study obtain evidence capable of answering the question and supporting the intended claim?</blockquote>
          <div class="component-grid architecture-components" aria-label="Eight decisions coordinated by research design">
            <article><span>01</span><strong>Purpose and problem</strong></article>
            <article><span>02</span><strong>Framework and assumptions</strong></article>
            <article><span>03</span><strong>Research questions</strong></article>
            <article><span>04</span><strong>Intended claims</strong></article>
            <article><span>05</span><strong>Design family and timing</strong></article>
            <article><span>06</span><strong>Cases, participants or data</strong></article>
            <article><span>07</span><strong>Sampling and access</strong></article>
            <article><span>08</span><strong>Quality and ethics</strong></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway design-architecture-takeaway">A design is not simply “qualitative,” “quantitative,” a survey or an interview. Changing one decision may require changes elsewhere; alignment is a property of the system.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究設計協調<br />整項研究</h2>
          <blockquote class="design-architecture-question">本研究將如何取得能夠回答問題並支持預期主張的證據？</blockquote>
          <div class="component-grid architecture-components" aria-label="研究設計協調的八項決策">
            <article><span>01</span><strong>目的與研究課題</strong></article>
            <article><span>02</span><strong>框架與假設</strong></article>
            <article><span>03</span><strong>研究問題</strong></article>
            <article><span>04</span><strong>預期主張</strong></article>
            <article><span>05</span><strong>設計類型與時序</strong></article>
            <article><span>06</span><strong>個案、參與者或資料</strong></article>
            <article><span>07</span><strong>抽樣與進入研究場域</strong></article>
            <article><span>08</span><strong>研究品質與倫理</strong></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway design-architecture-takeaway">研究設計不只是「質性」、「量化」、問卷或訪談。改變一項決策，可能需要同時調整其他決策；對齊是整個系統的特性。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Methodology, design and methods" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Do not collapse the levels</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Three related decisions</h2>
          <div class="grid-3 level-cards">
            <article class="panel accent"><span>WHY</span><h3>Methodology</h3><p>The rationale and principles governing how knowledge will be produced.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><span>ARCHITECTURE</span><h3>Research design</h3><p>The overall structure connecting questions, evidence, comparison, timing and inference.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><span>HOW</span><h3>Methods</h3><p>The procedures used to generate and analyse particular forms of data.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">“I will use interviews” states a method. It does not yet state or justify a research design.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>三個相關但不同的決策</h2>
          <div class="grid-3 level-cards">
            <article class="panel accent"><span>為何</span><h3>方法論</h3><p>規範研究如何產生知識的理據與原則。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><span>架構</span><h3>研究設計</h3><p>把研究問題、證據、比較、時序與推論連結起來的整體結構。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><span>如何</span><h3>方法</h3><p>產生及分析特定資料形式的程序。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">「我會進行訪談」只說明方法，尚未說明或論證研究設計。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Start with the intended claim" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Claim-led design</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>What kind of answer are you seeking?</h2>
          <div class="claim-ladder design-claims">
            <article><span>Describe</span><p>What exists, how often, for whom or in what form?</p></article>
            <article><span>Relate</span><p>Do variables, conditions or experiences vary together?</p></article>
            <article><span>Explain</span><p>How or why does a process, pattern or experience occur?</p></article>
            <article><span>Evaluate change</span><p>Did an intervention or condition contribute to an outcome?</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">The wording of the claim determines what comparison, variation, context and evidence the design must provide.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>你要尋找哪一類答案？</h2>
          <div class="claim-ladder design-claims">
            <article><span>描述</span><p>存在甚麼、頻率如何、涉及誰，或呈現甚麼形式？</p></article>
            <article><span>關聯</span><p>變項、條件或經驗是否共同變化？</p></article>
            <article><span>解釋</span><p>某個過程、模式或經驗如何或為何發生？</p></article>
            <article><span>評估改變</span><p>某項介入或條件是否促成結果？</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">主張的措辭決定研究設計必須提供甚麼比較、變異、情境與證據。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Design family map" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design landscape</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Begin with the question, not a favourite method</h2>
          <div class="design-family-map">
            <article><span>Pattern or estimate</span><strong>Descriptive / survey</strong></article>
            <article><span>Association or prediction</span><strong>Correlational</strong></article>
            <article><span>Difference or effect</span><strong>Experimental / quasi-experimental</strong></article>
            <article><span>Bounded complexity</span><strong>Case study</strong></article>
            <article><span>Meaning or experience</span><strong>Phenomenology / narrative</strong></article>
            <article><span>Culture, process or change</span><strong>Ethnography / grounded theory / action research</strong></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">These are families, not recipes. Each still requires decisions about context, sampling, evidence, timing and quality.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>從研究問題出發，而不是從偏好的方法出發</h2>
          <div class="design-family-map">
            <article><span>模式或估計</span><strong>描述性研究／調查</strong></article>
            <article><span>關聯或預測</span><strong>相關研究</strong></article>
            <article><span>差異或效果</span><strong>實驗／準實驗研究</strong></article>
            <article><span>有邊界的複雜性</span><strong>個案研究</strong></article>
            <article><span>意義或經驗</span><strong>現象學／敘事研究</strong></article>
            <article><span>文化、過程或改變</span><strong>民族誌／紮根理論／行動研究</strong></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">這些是設計類型，不是固定配方。每種設計仍需決定情境、抽樣、證據、時序及品質。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Descriptive and survey designs" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design family</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Describe a population, condition or pattern</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Best suited to</h3><p>Prevalence, distributions, characteristics, attitudes or reported practices.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Design decisions</h3><p>Target population, sampling frame, measurement quality and response coverage.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Claim boundary</h3><p>A one-time survey can describe or associate; it usually cannot establish that one variable caused another.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction"><strong>Ask:</strong> Whom should the estimate represent, and does the achieved sample support that scope?</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>描述群體、狀況或模式</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>適合回答</h3><p>盛行率、分布、特徵、態度或自陳實踐。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>設計決策</h3><p>目標群體、抽樣框、測量品質及回應覆蓋程度。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>主張邊界</h3><p>一次性調查可以描述或分析關聯，但通常不能確立一個變項造成另一個變項。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction"><strong>要問：</strong>估計結果應代表誰？實際取得的樣本能否支持這個範圍？</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Correlational and predictive designs" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design family</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Examine variation and association</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Best suited to</h3><p>Whether variables move together and whether one set helps predict another.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Design decisions</h3><p>Construct definition, temporal ordering, plausible confounders and a justified model.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Claim boundary</h3><p>Prediction is not automatically explanation; association is not automatically causation.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction"><strong>Ask:</strong> Which alternative explanation could produce the same observed association?</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>檢視變異與關聯</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>適合回答</h3><p>變項是否共同變化，以及一組變項能否協助預測另一組變項。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>設計決策</h3><p>構念定義、時間先後、可能的混淆因素及有理據的模型。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>主張邊界</h3><p>預測不等於解釋；關聯也不等於因果。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="instruction"><strong>要問：</strong>哪個其他解釋也可能產生同樣的關聯？</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Experimental and quasi-experimental designs" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design family</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Estimate whether an intervention contributes to change</h2>
          <div class="contrast design-comparison">
            <article><h3>Experiment</h3><p>Manipulates a condition and uses random assignment where feasible to strengthen group comparability.</p></article>
            <b>↔</b>
            <article><h3>Quasi-experiment</h3><p>Examines an intervention without random assignment and must address pre-existing differences explicitly.</p></article>
          </div>
          <div class="evidence-strip"><span>Comparison</span><span>Before/after evidence</span><span>Implementation fidelity</span><span>Alternative explanations</span></div>
          <p class="takeaway">A pre-test and post-test alone do not prove that the intervention caused the change.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>估計介入是否促成改變</h2>
          <div class="contrast design-comparison">
            <article><h3>實驗研究</h3><p>操弄條件，並在可行情況下隨機分派，以提高組別的可比較性。</p></article>
            <b>↔</b>
            <article><h3>準實驗研究</h3><p>在沒有隨機分派下檢視介入，因此必須明確處理原有組別差異。</p></article>
          </div>
          <div class="evidence-strip"><span>比較</span><span>前後證據</span><span>實施忠實度</span><span>其他解釋</span></div>
          <p class="takeaway">只有前測與後測，並不足以證明介入造成改變。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Case study design" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design family</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Study a bounded case in context</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>The case</h3><p>A person, programme, class, school, event or organisation.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>The boundary</h3><p>Define the place, period, participants and activity included.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>The evidence</h3><p>Use multiple relevant sources to understand the case, not merely one interview.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>The claim</h3><p>Explain the case deeply; do not treat it as a statistical sample of all cases.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">“A case study” must identify what the case is and where its boundary lies.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>在情境中研究一個有明確邊界的個案</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>個案</h3><p>個人、課程、班級、學校、事件或組織。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>邊界</h3><p>界定納入的地點、時期、參與者與活動。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>證據</h3><p>使用多種相關來源理解個案，而不只是進行一次訪談。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>主張</h3><p>深入解釋個案，不把個案當成所有個案的統計樣本。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">使用「個案研究」時，必須清楚指出個案是甚麼，以及邊界在哪裡。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Phenomenology and narrative research" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design family</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Experience and story are not the same object</h2>
          <div class="contrast design-comparison">
            <article><h3>Phenomenology</h3><p>Investigates how people experience and make meaning of a shared phenomenon.</p><strong>Focus:</strong> the structure and meaning of lived experience.</article>
            <b>↔</b>
            <article><h3>Narrative research</h3><p>Investigates how people construct and communicate experience through stories.</p><strong>Focus:</strong> sequence, turning points, voice and context.</article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Both may use interviews, but the analytic object and intended account differ.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>經驗與故事並不是同一研究對象</h2>
          <div class="contrast design-comparison">
            <article><h3>現象學</h3><p>探討人們如何經歷共同現象並賦予其意義。</p><strong>焦點：</strong>生活經驗的結構與意義。</article>
            <b>↔</b>
            <article><h3>敘事研究</h3><p>探討人們如何透過故事建構及表達經驗。</p><strong>焦點：</strong>時序、轉折點、聲音與情境。</article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">兩者都可能使用訪談，但分析對象與預期產出的解釋不同。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Ethnography, grounded theory and action research" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design family</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Choose according to the object and purpose</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Ethnography</h3><p>Understand practices, meanings and relationships within a cultural or social setting through sustained engagement.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Grounded theory</h3><p>Develop a process-oriented theoretical account through iterative data collection, comparison and analysis.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Action research</h3><p>Investigate and improve practice through planned cycles of action, evidence and reflection with relevant participants.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">The label must change how the study is organised. It is not a decorative synonym for “qualitative.”</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>根據研究對象與目的作出選擇</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>民族誌</h3><p>透過持續參與，理解文化或社會場域中的實踐、意義與關係。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>紮根理論</h3><p>透過反覆蒐集資料、比較及分析，發展以過程為核心的理論解釋。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>行動研究</h3><p>與相關參與者透過行動、證據及反思的規劃循環，研究並改善實踐。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">設計名稱必須改變研究的組織方式，不能只是「質性研究」的裝飾性同義詞。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Mixed methods: the entry question" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Design family · Preview only</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Does the problem require both forms of evidence?</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Quantitative contribution</h3><p>Magnitude, distribution, comparison, association or change.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Qualitative contribution</h3><p>Meaning, mechanism, experience, process or contextual explanation.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Integration requirement</h3><p>The strands must inform one another and support a combined inference.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Two datasets do not automatically make mixed-methods research. Use both only when a single approach leaves a consequential gap.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究課題是否同時需要兩種證據？</h2>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>量化貢獻</h3><p>幅度、分布、比較、關聯或改變。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>質性貢獻</h3><p>意義、機制、經驗、過程或情境解釋。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>整合要求</h3><p>兩個研究部分必須互相提供資訊，並支持綜合推論。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">擁有兩組資料不等於混合方法研究。只有當單一取向留下重要缺口時，才應同時使用兩者。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Design decision path" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">A repeatable decision sequence</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Ask these questions in order</h2>
          <ol class="decision-list">
            <li><strong>What must be understood or claimed?</strong><span>Describe, relate, explain, evaluate or predict?</span></li>
            <li><strong>What variation or context must be observed?</strong><span>Across people, settings, conditions, events or time?</span></li>
            <li><strong>What comparison is necessary?</strong><span>No comparison, within-case, between groups, before/after or across phases?</span></li>
            <li><strong>What evidence could challenge the preferred answer?</strong><span>Plan for alternatives, negative cases and rival explanations.</span></li>
            <li><strong>What design can be implemented ethically and well?</strong><span>A modest coherent design is stronger than an ambitious incoherent one.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>依次提出這些問題</h2>
          <ol class="decision-list">
            <li><strong>研究必須理解或主張甚麼？</strong><span>描述、關聯、解釋、評估，還是預測？</span></li>
            <li><strong>必須觀察甚麼變異或情境？</strong><span>跨個人、場域、條件、事件，還是時間？</span></li>
            <li><strong>需要甚麼比較？</strong><span>不比較、個案內、組別間、前後，還是跨階段？</span></li>
            <li><strong>甚麼證據可能挑戰偏好的答案？</strong><span>預先考慮其他解釋、反例與負面個案。</span></li>
            <li><strong>哪個設計能在倫理上妥善實施？</strong><span>規模適中而連貫的設計，勝過宏大但失去對齊的設計。</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 2: Design Match" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 2</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Design Match</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Choose the most defensible starting design. More information could change the decision, so justify every match.</p>
          <div class="interactive-stack compact-activity" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>How common is generative-AI use among doctoral students across the university?</p><select data-answer="survey"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="survey">Descriptive survey</option><option value="case">Case study</option><option value="experiment">Experiment</option><option value="phenom">Phenomenology</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Does a structured feedback intervention improve revision quality compared with usual practice?</p><select data-answer="experiment"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="survey">Descriptive survey</option><option value="case">Case study</option><option value="experiment">Experiment / quasi-experiment</option><option value="phenom">Phenomenology</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>How do first-generation doctoral students experience belonging during their first year?</p><select data-answer="phenom"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="survey">Descriptive survey</option><option value="case">Case study</option><option value="experiment">Experiment</option><option value="phenom">Phenomenology</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>How did one school implement and adapt a multilingual assessment policy?</p><select data-answer="case"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="survey">Descriptive survey</option><option value="case">Case study</option><option value="experiment">Experiment</option><option value="phenom">Phenomenology</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>Check matches</button><button type="button" data-clear>Clear</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究設計配對</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">選擇最站得住腳的初步設計。更多資料可能改變決定，因此每項配對都需要理據。</p>
          <div class="interactive-stack compact-activity" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>全校博士生使用生成式人工智能的情況有多普遍？</p><select data-answer="survey"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="survey">描述性調查</option><option value="case">個案研究</option><option value="experiment">實驗研究</option><option value="phenom">現象學</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>與一般做法相比，結構化回饋介入能否改善修訂品質？</p><select data-answer="experiment"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="survey">描述性調查</option><option value="case">個案研究</option><option value="experiment">實驗／準實驗研究</option><option value="phenom">現象學</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>第一代大學生背景的博士生如何經歷第一年的歸屬感？</p><select data-answer="phenom"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="survey">描述性調查</option><option value="case">個案研究</option><option value="experiment">實驗研究</option><option value="phenom">現象學</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>某一所學校如何實施及調整多語評估政策？</p><select data-answer="case"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="survey">描述性調查</option><option value="case">個案研究</option><option value="experiment">實驗研究</option><option value="phenom">現象學</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>檢查配對</button><button type="button" data-clear>清除</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 3: Design Clinic" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 3</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Design Clinic</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Diagnose the problem before opening each card. Then compare your repair with the suggested response.</p>
          <div class="debug-grid">
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>A one-time survey concludes that AI use causes stronger research confidence.</summary><p>The design establishes association, not causal direction. Revise the claim or add temporal evidence, a defensible comparison and control of alternative explanations.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>Ten purposively selected interviewees are used to estimate university-wide prevalence.</summary><p>Information-rich purposive sampling can support depth, not a population estimate. Revise the question or adopt a probability-based sampling plan.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>A survey and interviews are conducted, then reported in separate chapters and called mixed methods.</summary><p>The study is merely additive unless the strands answer connected questions and contribute to a planned combined inference.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>The paper says “case study” but never identifies the case or its boundary.</summary><p>Define the bounded case, context, period and units; explain why the case is informative and which evidence is needed to understand it.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>A study selects grounded theory because it includes interview coding.</summary><p>Coding interviews does not make grounded theory. The design requires iterative sampling and analysis directed towards developing a theoretical account.</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>The preferred design requires access that the researcher is unlikely to obtain.</summary><p>Feasibility is a design condition. Narrow the setting, change the unit or select an alternative design that can still answer the core question well.</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究設計診所</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">打開卡片前先診斷問題，再把你的修正與建議答案比較。</p>
          <div class="debug-grid">
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>一次性調查得出「使用人工智能會造成更強研究信心」的結論。</summary><p>該設計只能建立關聯，不能確立因果方向。應修訂主張，或加入時間證據、有理據的比較及對其他解釋的控制。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>以十名目的抽樣的受訪者估計全校盛行率。</summary><p>目的抽樣可取得資訊豐富的深度證據，但不能支持群體估計。應修訂問題，或採用以機率為基礎的抽樣計劃。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>研究同時進行問卷與訪談，分章報告後便稱為混合方法。</summary><p>若兩個部分沒有回答互相連結的問題，也沒有支持預先規劃的綜合推論，研究只是在方法上相加。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>論文稱為「個案研究」，卻沒有指出個案及其邊界。</summary><p>應界定有邊界的個案、情境、時期及分析單位；解釋個案為何有資訊價值，以及需要哪些證據理解它。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>研究因為包含訪談編碼而選擇紮根理論。</summary><p>編碼訪談並不等於紮根理論。該設計需要以發展理論解釋為目標，反覆進行抽樣與分析。</p></details>
            <details class="debug-card"><summary>偏好的設計需要研究者不太可能取得的場域進入權限。</summary><p>可行性是設計條件。應縮小場域、改變分析單位，或選擇仍能妥善回答核心問題的替代設計。</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Sampling foundations" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Sampling</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Define what is being sampled before choosing how</h2>
          <div class="sampling-stack">
            <article><strong>Unit of analysis</strong><span>What entity will the claims describe?</span></article>
            <article><strong>Target population or phenomenon</strong><span>To whom or what should the claim apply?</span></article>
            <article><strong>Accessible population or field</strong><span>What can the researcher realistically reach?</span></article>
            <article><strong>Sampling frame and criteria</strong><span>How will eligible people, cases, texts, events or settings be identified?</span></article>
            <article><strong>Achieved sample</strong><span>Who or what actually contributes usable evidence?</span></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">The sample is not always people. It may include classrooms, documents, interactions, events, sites or time periods.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>先界定抽取甚麼，再決定如何抽樣</h2>
          <div class="sampling-stack">
            <article><strong>分析單位</strong><span>主張將描述哪一種實體？</span></article>
            <article><strong>目標群體或現象</strong><span>主張應適用於誰或甚麼？</span></article>
            <article><strong>可接觸群體或場域</strong><span>研究者實際能接觸甚麼？</span></article>
            <article><strong>抽樣框與準則</strong><span>如何辨識符合資格的人、個案、文本、事件或場域？</span></article>
            <article><strong>實際樣本</strong><span>最終由誰或甚麼提供可用證據？</span></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">樣本不一定是人，也可以是課堂、文件、互動、事件、場域或時段。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Probability sampling" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Sampling logic</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Probability sampling supports population inference</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Simple random</h3><p>Every unit has a known, non-zero selection chance through a random procedure.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Systematic</h3><p>Select every kth unit after a random starting point, if the list has no harmful pattern.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Stratified</h3><p>Sample within meaningful subgroups to protect representation or improve precision.</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>Cluster / multistage</h3><p>Select natural groups, then possibly sample units within selected groups.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Random selection is about how units enter the sample. It is not the same as random assignment to conditions.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>機率抽樣支持群體推論</h2>
          <div class="grid-4">
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>簡單隨機抽樣</h3><p>每個單位都透過隨機程序，擁有已知且非零的入選機會。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>系統抽樣</h3><p>隨機決定起點後，每隔第 k 個單位抽取一次，前提是名單沒有造成偏差的規律。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>分層抽樣</h3><p>在有意義的子群內抽樣，以保障代表性或提高估計精確度。</p></article>
            <article class="panel accent"><h3>叢集／多階段抽樣</h3><p>先選取自然群組，再視需要於入選群組內抽取單位。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">隨機抽樣關乎單位如何進入樣本，並不等同於把參與者隨機分派至不同條件。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Non-probability sampling" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Sampling logic</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Select for access, composition or information</h2>
          <div class="grid-6">
            <article class="panel"><h3>Convenience</h3><p>Use readily accessible units.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Volunteer</h3><p>Participants self-select after an invitation.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Purposive</h3><p>Select cases relevant to the research purpose.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Snowball</h3><p>Participants help reach others in a network.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Quota</h3><p>Fill planned subgroup categories without random selection.</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Theoretical</h3><p>Select further cases to develop an emerging theoretical account.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">Non-probability does not mean careless. State the selection logic and limit claims to what it can support.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>按可接觸性、組成或資訊價值選取</h2>
          <div class="grid-6">
            <article class="panel"><h3>便利抽樣</h3><p>使用容易接觸的單位。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>志願者抽樣</h3><p>參與者回應邀請後自行選擇加入。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>目的抽樣</h3><p>選取與研究目的相關的個案。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>滾雪球抽樣</h3><p>由參與者協助接觸其網絡中的其他人。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>配額抽樣</h3><p>在沒有隨機選取下填滿預定子群類別。</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>理論抽樣</h3><p>為發展正在形成的理論解釋而選取後續個案。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">非機率抽樣不等於隨意。必須說明選取邏輯，並把主張限制在該邏輯能支持的範圍內。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Sample adequacy" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Sampling logic</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>There is no universal “good sample size”</h2>
          <div class="contrast design-comparison">
            <article><h3>Quantitative adequacy</h3><p>Depends on the target inference, expected variation or effect, precision, design structure, planned analysis and likely missingness.</p></article>
            <b>↔</b>
            <article><h3>Qualitative adequacy</h3><p>Depends on the design, specificity of participants, richness and relevance of evidence, variation sought and depth of analysis.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">“Large” is not automatically representative; “small” is not automatically inadequate. Justify adequacy for the question and design.</p>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>並不存在通用的「良好樣本量」</h2>
          <div class="contrast design-comparison">
            <article><h3>量化研究的充分性</h3><p>取決於目標推論、預期變異或效果、精確度、設計結構、計劃分析及可能的缺失資料。</p></article>
            <b>↔</b>
            <article><h3>質性研究的充分性</h3><p>取決於研究設計、參與者的特定性、證據的豐富與相關程度、所需差異及分析深度。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="takeaway">「大」不一定具有代表性，「小」也不一定不充分。應根據研究問題與設計論證其充分性。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 4: Sampling Match" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 4</span></header>
        <div data-language="en">
          <h2>Sampling Match</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Match the selection procedure to the sampling strategy.</p>
          <div class="interactive-stack compact-activity" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Randomly select four schools, then randomly select students within each school.</p><select data-answer="multistage"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="stratified">Stratified</option><option value="purposive">Purposive</option><option value="multistage">Multistage</option><option value="snowball">Snowball</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Select teachers who have implemented bilingual assessment for at least two years.</p><select data-answer="purposive"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="stratified">Stratified</option><option value="purposive">Purposive</option><option value="multistage">Multistage</option><option value="snowball">Snowball</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Randomly sample within school level so primary and secondary schools are both represented.</p><select data-answer="stratified"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="stratified">Stratified</option><option value="purposive">Purposive</option><option value="multistage">Multistage</option><option value="snowball">Snowball</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>Ask participants in a hard-to-reach professional network to refer eligible colleagues.</p><select data-answer="snowball"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="stratified">Stratified</option><option value="purposive">Purposive</option><option value="multistage">Multistage</option><option value="snowball">Snowball</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>Check matches</button><button type="button" data-clear>Clear</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>抽樣配對</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">把選取程序配對至相應抽樣策略。</p>
          <div class="interactive-stack compact-activity" data-check-activity>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>隨機選取四所學校，再於每所學校內隨機抽取學生。</p><select data-answer="multistage"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="stratified">分層抽樣</option><option value="purposive">目的抽樣</option><option value="multistage">多階段抽樣</option><option value="snowball">滾雪球抽樣</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>選取已有至少兩年雙語評估實施經驗的教師。</p><select data-answer="purposive"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="stratified">分層抽樣</option><option value="purposive">目的抽樣</option><option value="multistage">多階段抽樣</option><option value="snowball">滾雪球抽樣</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>在不同學校階段內隨機抽樣，以確保小學與中學均有代表。</p><select data-answer="stratified"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="stratified">分層抽樣</option><option value="purposive">目的抽樣</option><option value="multistage">多階段抽樣</option><option value="snowball">滾雪球抽樣</option></select></div>
            <div class="sort-row"><p>請難以接觸的專業網絡中的參與者轉介符合資格的同事。</p><select data-answer="snowball"><option value="">請選擇⋯⋯</option><option value="stratified">分層抽樣</option><option value="purposive">目的抽樣</option><option value="multistage">多階段抽樣</option><option value="snowball">滾雪球抽樣</option></select></div>
            <div class="activity-actions"><button type="button" data-check>檢查配對</button><button type="button" data-clear>清除</button><span class="activity-status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
